    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## How this works\n**Three triggers, one pipeline.** Only one fires per run:\n- **Every day at 07:00** and **When n8n starts or is published** both go through **Daily run due?**. It lets a run through only after 07:00 and only if today's run hasn't happened yet, so a missed 07:00 run happens as soon as n8n is back.\n- **Read emails on demand** (form): last N days, or all emails. Always runs.\n\n**Build Gmail search** turns `days` into `newer_than:Nd` (empty = everything). Each **Gmail** node runs it with its own credential and retries if the network isn't up yet.\n**Record run + clean up** marks today as done (daily runs only) in the workflow's static data.\n\n⚠️ Triggers and static data only work when the workflow is **Published**.",
        "height": 400,
        "width": 560
      },
      "id": "b1f6a0e2-0007-4c1a-9a10-000000000007",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -560
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "events": [
          "init",
          "activate",
          "update"
        ]
      },
      "id": "b1f6a0e2-0015-4c1a-9a10-000000000015",
      "name": "When n8n starts or is published",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.n8nTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        60
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Decides whether the daily run should happen now.\n// Static data survives restarts, but n8n only saves it for real runs of a\n// published workflow, not for tests in the editor.\nconst state = $getWorkflowStaticData('global');\nconst RUN_HOUR = 7;\nconst now = $now; // workflow timezone (Workflow settings → Timezone)\nconst today = now.toISODate();\nconst dueAt = now.startOf('day').set({ hour: RUN_HOUR });\nconst source = $input.first().json.event ? 'catch-up' : 'schedule';\n\nif (now < dueAt.minus({ minutes: 1 })) return []; // before 07:00: the schedule will handle it\nif (state.lastDailyRun === today) return [];      // already ran today\n\n// Normally 3 days. If n8n was off for longer, widen the window so no email is missed.\nlet days = 3;\nif (state.lastDailyRun) {\n  const last = DateTime.fromISO(state.lastDailyRun, { zone: now.zone });\n  days = Math.max(3, Math.round(now.startOf('day').diff(last, 'days').days) + 1);\n}\nreturn [{ json: { days, source, lastDailyRun: state.lastDailyRun ?? null } }];\n"
      },
      "id": "b1f6a0e2-0016-4c1a-9a10-000000000016",
      "name": "Daily run due?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        240,
        -30
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Runs last, so a daily run only counts as done if every step before it succeeded.\nconst { source } = $('Build Gmail search').first().json;\nif (source !== 'form') {\n  $getWorkflowStaticData('global').lastDailyRun = $now.toISODate();\n}\n// Drop the empty placeholder items Gmail outputs when an inbox has no matches.\nreturn $input.all().filter(item => item.json.id);"
      },
      "id": "b1f6a0e2-0017-4c1a-9a10-000000000017",
      "name": "Record run + clean up",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1440,
        120
      ]
    }
